※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4622 LANG_CONTAINER_OWNER_UNKNOWN

※ Text put into an array is copied into the array's allocator unless it was provably made there,
※ so an array whose allocator nothing says has nowhere to copy into: a parameter with no `in`.
※ `v: mut str⟦⟧ in a` says it.

@[impure]
fn put(v: mut str⟦⟧, s: str):
    v⟦0⟧ ← s

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let w: mut str⟦2⟧ = ⟦"a", "b"⟧
    put(w, "c")
    0u6
